# Ti - Ugur interatomic potential, hard truncation, the reference parameters
#
# pair_style ugur
# pair_coeff * * Ti.ugur Ti
#
# Truncation: hard - phi2 is cut at rcut2 and does NOT vanish there, so this set is for static properties, not dynamics
# MD: DO NOT USE.  At 600 K the crystal collapses: it reaches 304 K and its potential energy falls below the static lattice.  Static properties from this set are still valid.
#
# Nudge test: passed - displaced by 1e-5 A and relaxed, the lattice returns.
#
# Fitted to: cohesive energy, lattice constant, bulk modulus and the elastic
# constants of Ti at its experimental lattice constant.  Nothing else.
#
# Format is LAMMPS's Tersoff convention - one line per ordered triple
# (centre, leg, leg) - so that this file and a multi-element one are read the
# same way.  For a single element that is one line.
#
# el1 el2 el3  m D alpha r0 gamma C alpha3 rcut2 rcut3 taper lam2 lam4
Ti Ti Ti 7.4891514332797593 0.40749178916336154 0.54028403703049699 3.1139574071071308 3.4327394030672113e-06 -0.30810132956803299 0.66765786979430974 7.6715600000000004 4.3437309040412861 -1 0 0
